+    <!-- FacetUI: what a surface does when it cannot be glass.
+
+         Every FacetUI surface is translucent so the blur behind it shows
+         through. When there is no blur - battery saver, the developer option
+         "disable blurs", or a GPU that cannot afford it - the translucency is
+         left doing nothing useful and a good deal of harm, because a panel at
+         77% over unblurred scrolling content is harder to read than an opaque
+         one.
+
+         With this true, a surface that ASKED for background blur and did not
+         get it composites over an opaque layer of its own colour instead.
+         Surfaces that never wanted blur are untouched, so a genuinely
+         transparent window is not affected.
+
+         It also solidifies when high contrast text is enabled, which is the
+         closest thing Android has to a reduce-transparency setting.
+
+         false is stock behaviour. -->
+    <bool name="facetui_solidify_when_no_blur">false</bool>
 </resources>
